<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka loses early gains to close flat.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka loses early gains to close flat.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh taka lost early gains to close unchanged at 42.5380/42.5480 to the dollar in interbank trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>The taka quoted firmer at 42.5350/42.5450 on a weak demand for dollars in early trading. But the gains petered out later with banks seeking dollars for import payments.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates closed unchanged at 4.00 percent to 4.75 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
